## Note on a flake that was diagnosed, not re-rolled
The first combined run showed 1 failure that passed on re-run. Cause found, not retried away:
mutation run 6 made k122c throw, and its `finally { client.release() }` handed a connection
with an ABORTED transaction back to the pool, so a later checkout (in this file or the next)
got a bare 25P02, and afterAll's cleanup failed — leaving a K122c fixture company and 2
dunning_sends rows in the shared fixture DB. Fixed in the test: the error path now calls
`client.release(true)` to destroy the connection. Re-verified by re-running mutation 6 —
still RED, and 0 rows left behind. The orphaned rows were deleted by company_id (only my
own; K120/K126c fixtures belonging to other agents were left untouched).
